      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/i/df705f/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-06-25T06:43:19.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hello,</p><p>&nbsp;looked in the game book but it isn't defined. In GSF a card that you are playing is counted as being part of your hand or not ? Asking, because the definition isn't always the same depending on the game (in Pathfinder Card Game by example it would be). I am asking about the dwarf booster that count the number of boost in your hand.</p><p>Ike.</p>",
